    <bpmn:process id="W_W773" name="W773. Store-Level Customer Hold &amp; Will-Call Order Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests item be held for later pickup; or customer special order (W545) arrives and needs staging
Frequency: Daily; ~3–5 will-call orders per store per day
Volume: 200 stores × ~4 will-call orders/day = ~800 will-call orders/day chain-wide
Owner: Customer Service Rep
Participants: CSR, Stock Associate, Customer
Source: workflow W773 — Store-Level Customer Hold &amp; Will-Call Order Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W773_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W773_Lane1" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W773_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W773_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W773_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W773_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W773_Start6" name="Customer requests item be held for later pickup; or customer special order (W545) arrives…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W773_Task7" name="Hold request received">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Hold request received: Customer requests hold at customer service counter: (a) CSR verifies item availability per POS inventory, (b) confirms item is in sellable condition (not display unit per W524 unless customer agrees), (c) identifies customer via loyalty account or phone number
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): CSR
Duration: 3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W773_Task8" name="Hold creation in system">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Hold creation in system: CSR creates will-call hold order: (a) customer details (name, phone, email), (b) item SKU, quantity, and location, (c) hold expiry (standard: 24 hours; extended: 48 hours with Department Supervisor approval), (d) special instructions (e.g., &quot;customer will measure lumber to length&quot;), (e) no payment collected — hold is a reservation, not a sale
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): CSR
Duration: 3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W773_Task9" name="Inventory reservation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Inventory reservation: System creates soft hold on inventory: (a) removes held quantity from available-to-promise across all channels (POS, ecommerce, BOPIS), (b) physical item pulled from shelf by Stock Associate and placed in will-call staging area with hold tag showing customer name, hold number, and expiry date
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Stock Associate
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W773_Task10" name="Customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer notification: System sends confirmation to customer: &quot;Your item [SKU] has been held at [Store Name] until [Date/Time]. Please bring a valid ID for pickup. Hold reference: #[X].&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): CSR
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W773_Task11" name="Expiry monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Expiry monitoring: System monitors hold expiry: (a) 4 hours before expiry — reminder notification to customer, (b) at expiry — hold auto-cancelled if no pickup, (c) item returned to shelf and ATP restored
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): CSR
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W773_Task12" name="Customer pickup and sale completion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer pickup and sale completion: Customer arrives for pickup: (a) CSR retrieves item from will-call staging, (b) verifies customer identity, (c) processes sale transaction at current price (not price at time of hold — holds do not guarantee pricing unless rain check per W772), (d) system closes hold order and confirms sale
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): CSR
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W773_Task13" name="Expired hold restock">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Expired hold restock: For expired holds: (a) Stock Associate returns item to shelf per planogram (W86), (b) system releases inventory reservation, (c) CSR attempts to contact customer (one-time courtesy call), (d) no penalty or charge to customer for expired holds
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / CSR
Accountable (A): CSR
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W773_Task14" name="Weekly will-call analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly will-call analytics: Store Manager reviews: (a) hold-to-sale conversion rate (target &gt; 75%), (b) average hold duration, (c) expired hold rate, (d) items most frequently held (indicates possible planogram or inventory positioning improvement)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): CSR
Duration: 15 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W773_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W773_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W773_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W773_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-268 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Amenities &amp; Assistance (PA-09.3).) | - operational: must enforce inventory reservation across all channels
Owner: Customer Service Rep</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W773_Assoc17" sourceRef="W773_Annotation16" targetRef="W773_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W773_Flow18" sourceRef="W773_Start6" targetRef="W773_Task7" />
