    <bpmn:process id="W_W1162" name="W1162. Store-Level Customer Power Tool &amp; Equipment Pre-Purchase Try-Before-You-Buy Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer expresses interest in a power tool or equipment purchase but wants to test before committing, or customer inquires about tool demo, or sales associate identifies high-value equipment opportunity
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 try-before-you-buy sessions/month across all stores
Volume: 1–2 tools per session
Owner: Department Supervisor (Tools &amp; Hardware)
Participants: Sales Associate (Tools Department), Customer, Tool Demo Station Attendant
Source: workflow W1162 — Store-Level Customer Power Tool &amp; Equipment Pre-Purchase Try-Before-You-Buy Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1162_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1162_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1162_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1162_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1162_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1162_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1162_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1162_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1162_Lane3" name="Demo Station Attendant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1162_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1162_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1162_Start5" name="Customer expresses interest in a power tool or equipment purchase but wants to test…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1162_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1162_Task6" name="Customer Need Assessment &amp; Tool Selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Need Assessment &amp; Tool Selection: (a) customer approaches tools department or is identified by sales associate browsing power tools; (b) associate assesses customer needs: professional contractor (daily use, durability priority), serious DIYer (weekly use, value priority), first-time buyer (ease of use priority); (c) associate recommends 2–3 tool options based on needs and budget: cordless drill (DeWalt vs. Makita vs. Bosch), circular saw, angle grinder, rotary hammer, etc.; (d) associate explains try-before-you-buy program: &quot;You can test any of these tools at our demo station before purchasing. I&#x27;ll set up the tools and safety gear for you.&quot;
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1162_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1162_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1162_Task7" name="Demo Station Setup &amp; Safety Briefing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Demo Station Setup &amp; Safety Briefing: (a) associate guides customer to dedicated tool demo station (equipped with workbench, scrap wood, test materials, power supply, and safety barriers); (b) associate retrieves selected tools from demo inventory (separate from sale stock — clearly marked &quot;DEMO UNIT&quot;); (c) safety briefing: safety glasses and ear protection donned, hair and loose clothing secured, safe handling instructions provided (&quot;Keep both hands on the tool. Never carry a plugged-in tool with finger on trigger. Unplug before changing bits/blades.&quot;); (d) customer signs safety acknowledgment per W749 (power tool safety acknowledgment); (e) demo materials prepared: scrap wood boards (for drills, saws, sanders), metal pipe sections (for grinders), concrete block (for rotary hammers)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Demo Station Attendant
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1162_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1162_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1162_Task8" name="Hands-On Testing &amp; Performance Comparison">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Hands-On Testing &amp; Performance Comparison: (a) customer tests each tool under associate guidance: cordless drill — drive screws into wood, drill holes, feel torque and speed settings, check weight and balance, evaluate trigger feel; circular saw — make cuts in plywood and 2×4 lumber, evaluate cutting speed, blade visibility, dust extraction; angle grinder — cut metal pipe, evaluate cutting speed and vibration; (b) associate facilitates comparison: &quot;Notice how the DeWalt has a tighter grip but the Makita is lighter. The Bosch has more speed settings. Which feels most comfortable for the kind of work you do?&quot;; (c) if battery-powered: associate demonstrates battery swap, checks battery life indicator, shows charger; (d) associate answers questions about warranty (W33), service center (W440), and accessory compatibility (W971)
Responsible (R): Customer / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1162_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1162_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1162_Task9" name="Purchase Conversion &amp; Demo-to-Sale Transition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Purchase Conversion &amp; Demo-to-Sale Transition: (a) after testing, associate asks: &quot;Which tool feels right for you?&quot;; (b) if customer selects a tool: associate retrieves new-in-box unit from shelf (NOT the demo unit); (c) associate verifies all accessories included (case, battery, charger, manual, warranty card); (d) processes sale at POS with safety acknowledgment per W749; (e) if customer needs time to decide: offers to hold a unit for 24 hours; (f) demo unit returned to demo station; (g) if customer declines all tested tools: feedback captured — &quot;What didn&#x27;t you like?&quot; → feeds into product assortment review (W1)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1162_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1162_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1162_Task10" name="Demo Unit Lifecycle Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Demo Unit Lifecycle Management: (a) demo units tracked separately in inventory: &quot;Demo — Not for Sale&quot; status; (b) demo units replaced every 3–6 months depending on wear; (c) retired demo units sold at discount per W524 (demo/display unit selling) with appropriate condition disclosure; (d) new demo unit ordered from vendor as replacement — often provided at deep discount or free by vendor for promotional purposes; (e) demo station maintained per W607 (demo station daily operations): tools cleaned, blades/bits replaced, safety gear inspected
Responsible (R): Demo Station Attendant / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–20 min/day maintenance</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1162_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1162_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1162_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1162_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1162_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-268 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Amenities &amp; Assistance (PA-09.3).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Tools &amp; Hardware) review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Tools &amp; Hardware)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1162_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1162_Annotation12" targetRef="W1162_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
