    <bpmn:process id="W_W1285" name="W1285. Customer Tile &amp; Flooring Sample Loan Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests to borrow tile or flooring samples for home color/pattern matching
Frequency: ~30–50 sample loan requests per store per month; ~6,000–10,000 chain-wide
Volume: ~2–4 samples per request; average loan duration 5–7 days; ~85% return rate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Tiles &amp; Flooring)
Participants: Sales Associate, Department Supervisor, Customer
Source: workflow W1285 — Customer Tile &amp; Flooring Sample Loan Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1285_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1285_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1285_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1285_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1285_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1285_Start5" name="Customer requests to borrow tile or flooring samples for home color/pattern matching">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1285_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1285_Task6" name="Customer sample request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer sample request: Customer visits tile gallery and selects 2–4 tiles/flooring samples they want to borrow; Sales Associate explains loan terms: (a) loan period: 7 days maximum, (b) refundable deposit per sample (PHP 100–500 depending on sample value), (c) samples must be returned in original condition, (d) loyalty members get 1 free sample loan per quarter (deposit waived)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1285_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1285_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1285_Task7" name="Sample loan registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sample loan registration: Sales Associate processes sample loan in ERP: (a) select sample item(s) from inventory (tile samples tracked as separate &quot;sample&quot; SKUs), (b) scan customer loyalty card or record guest details (name, phone, email), (c) system generates sample loan agreement with return deadline, (d) collect refundable deposit via POS (posted as customer deposit, not revenue), (e) customer signs loan agreement (digital signature on tablet)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1285_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1285_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1285_Task8" name="Sample loan tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Sample loan tracking: System tracks all active sample loans: (a) loan date, return deadline, customer details, sample items, deposit amount, (b) auto-reminder SMS/email to customer 2 days before return deadline, (c) if not returned by deadline: system flags overdue loan and sends follow-up SMS, (d) if not returned within 14 days: deposit forfeited, sample written off as consumed
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1285_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1285_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1285_Task9" name="Sample return processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Sample return processing: Customer returns samples to tile gallery: (a) Sales Associate inspects returned samples for damage (chips, scratches, stains), (b) if in good condition: process return in system, issue deposit refund via POS (cash or credit back to original payment method), (c) if damaged: deduct replacement cost from deposit, refund balance, (d) returned samples restocked in gallery display
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1285_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1285_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1285_Task10" name="Purchase conversion follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Purchase conversion follow-up: When customer returns samples, Sales Associate asks about purchase decision: (a) if customer decided: assist with order placement (full quantity order per W112 for trade accounts or standard sale), (b) if still deciding: offer additional sample options or schedule in-home consultation per W138, (c) if purchased elsewhere: record reason in CRM for competitive intelligence per W1278
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1285_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1285_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1285_Task11" name="Sample inventory management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Sample inventory management: Department Supervisor manages tile sample inventory: (a) maintain 2–3 display samples per SKU plus 3–5 loanable samples per popular SKU, (b) reorder depleted samples from vendor via sample PO (typically free or nominal cost from vendor), (c) refresh display samples that are shop-worn (every 3–6 months), (d) seasonal rotation: add new collection samples, remove discontinued items
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1285_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1285_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1285_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1285_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1285_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-268 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Amenities &amp; Assistance (PA-09.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Department Supervisor (Tiles &amp; Flooring)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1285_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1285_Annotation13" targetRef="W1285_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1285_Flow15" sourceRef="W1285_Start5" targetRef="W1285_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1285_Flow16" sourceRef="W1285_Task6" targetRef="W1285_Task7" />
