    <bpmn:process id="W_W2744" name="W2744. Customer Emergency Repair &amp; Urgent Need Rapid-Fulfillment Assistance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer arrives at store with an urgent repair need (burst pipe, broken lock, electrical outage, storm damage, broken window) and needs immediate help finding the right parts
Frequency: ~5–10 emergency requests per store per day; ~1,000–2,000 chain-wide daily
Volume: Peaks during typhoon season (June–November) and holiday periods
Owner: Sales Associate
Participants: Sales Associate, Department Supervisor, Customer, Store Manager (express checkout override if needed)
Source: workflow W2744 — Customer Emergency Repair &amp; Urgent Need Rapid-Fulfillment Assistance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W2744_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W2744_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2744_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W2744_Start3" name="Customer arrives at store with an urgent repair need (burst pipe, broken lock, electrical…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2744_Task4" name="Sales Associate identifies emergency repair customer by urgency cues: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sales Associate identifies emergency repair customer by urgency cues: (a) customer states urgency (&quot;I have a burst pipe,&quot; &quot;My roof is leaking right now&quot;); (b) customer carries a broken part or photo; (c) customer appears stressed or rushed; (d) Associate prioritizes emergency customer over browsing assistance
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2744_Task5" name="Sales Associate performs rapid needs assessment: (a) what is the problem? (b)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sales Associate performs rapid needs assessment: (a) what is the problem? (b) where is it located? (c) what type of material/system is involved? (d) does customer have the broken part or a photo? (e) what is the repair goal (temporary fix, permanent repair)?
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2744_Task6" name="If customer has the broken part or photo: (a) Associate visually matches the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: If customer has the broken part or photo: (a) Associate visually matches the part to stock items in the relevant department; (b) for plumbing: matches pipe diameter, fitting type (elbow, tee, coupling), material (PVC, PPR, galvanized); (c) for electrical: matches wire gauge, switch type, breaker amperage; (d) for locks: matches lock type, backset, handing; (e) if exact match not available: Associate identifies closest compatible substitute
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2744_Task7" name="If customer has no part or photo and cannot describe the item: (a) Associate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If customer has no part or photo and cannot describe the item: (a) Associate uses guided troubleshooting on tablet: &quot;Is the pipe plastic or metal? What diameter? Is it a supply line or drain?&quot;; (b) Associate uses photo reference library of common plumbing, electrical, and hardware parts for visual matching; (c) if still uncertain: Associate involves Department Supervisor with trade expertise
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2744_Task8" name="Associate gathers all needed items for the repair: (a) primary repair part(s)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Associate gathers all needed items for the repair: (a) primary repair part(s); (b) associated consumables (pipe cement, Teflon tape, wire nuts, screws, sealant); (c) safety items if needed (gloves for handling broken glass, electrical tape for wire repair); (d) Associate proactively includes items the customer may not think of (putty for sink repair, silicone for waterproofing)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2744_Task9" name="Express checkout: (a) Associate escorts emergency customer to the front of the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Express checkout: (a) Associate escorts emergency customer to the front of the checkout queue; (b) Cashier processes transaction with priority; (c) if customer is a trade account holder: applies account pricing per W5B.4c; (d) for emergency purchases during peak hours: Store Manager may authorize mPOS queue-busting per W206 for immediate checkout on the sales floor
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W2744_Task10" name="If the needed part is not in stock at this store: (a) system checks real-time…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: If the needed part is not in stock at this store: (a) system checks real-time availability at nearest BuildRight store; (b) if available nearby: Associate provides customer with store address, item SKU, and stock confirmation; calls ahead to hold item per W773; (c) if no nearby stock: Associate identifies special order option per W38 with estimated lead time; (d) for true emergencies (active water leak, electrical hazard): Store Manager contacts nearby competitor to check availability as a customer service gesture (not a sale but builds trust)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2744_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W2744_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W2744_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W2744_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-268 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Amenities &amp; Assistance (PA-09.3).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Sales Associate</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
