    <bpmn:process id="W_W1493" name="W1493. Store-Level Contractor Lounge &amp; Trade Amenities Management, Satisfaction Survey &amp; Retention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Contractor checks into store via loyalty app or in-store kiosk; also monthly amenity review cycle and quarterly trade customer satisfaction survey
Frequency: Daily contractor visits (~20–40 per store per day); monthly amenity review; quarterly satisfaction survey
Volume: contractor visits daily across the chain; ~5,200 active trade accounts plus ~200 corporate accounts (per profile §9.2)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Trade Account Manager (Store-Level), CSR, Department Supervisor, Loyalty Program Coordinator (HQ)
Source: workflow W1493 — Store-Level Contractor Lounge &amp; Trade Amenities Management, Satisfaction Survey &amp; Retention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1493_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1493_Lane1" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1493_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1493_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1493_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1493_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1493_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1493_Lane3" name="Loyalty Program Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1493_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1493_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1493_Start5" name="Contractor checks into store via loyalty app or in-store kiosk; also monthly amenity…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1493_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1493_Task6" name="Contractor check-in &amp; lounge access">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Contractor check-in &amp; lounge access: (a) contractor arrives at store and checks in via: (i) BuildRight mobile app (geofenced to store location); (ii) in-store kiosk scan of loyalty card; (b) system recognizes trade account tier and grants lounge access: (i) Silver tier: access during business hours; (ii) Gold tier: access including early-bird hours (6 AM, 1 hour before store opens); (iii) Platinum tier: dedicated workspace + priority service counter; (c) contractor receives personalized greeting on digital display in lounge area (if Platinum); (d) CSR monitors lounge capacity (max 15–20 persons depending on store) and manages access during peak hours
Responsible (R): CSR / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 min per check-in</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1493_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1493_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1493_Task7" name="Daily lounge amenity restocking &amp; maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily lounge amenity restocking &amp; maintenance: Daily: (a) CSR checks lounge supplies: coffee machine operation, coffee/water/sugar/cups stock, WiFi connectivity, cleanliness of seating and tables, restroom hygiene; (b) replenishes consumables from store stock; (c) reports any equipment issues (coffee machine malfunction, WiFi down, AC not working) to maintenance per PA-20.3; (d) lounge cleanliness checked every 2 hours during peak (7–10 AM, 12–2 PM); (e) daily amenity cost tracked: coffee, water, electricity, WiFi — target PHP 200–400/store/day
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1493_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1493_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1493_Task8" name="Monthly amenity performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly amenity performance review: Monthly: (a) Store Manager reviews lounge utilization metrics: (i) check-ins per day; (ii) average dwell time; (iii) amenity consumption cost vs. budget; (iv) trade account sales in stores with lounge vs. stores without; (b) amenity cost-per-trade-customer-visit calculated (target: PHP 20–40); (c) underperforming amenities identified (e.g., WiFi rarely used, coffee consumption low) and adjusted; (d) feedback from contractor conversations logged for HQ Loyalty Program Coordinator
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1493_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1493_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1493_Task9" name="Quarterly trade customer satisfaction survey">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly trade customer satisfaction survey: Quarterly: (a) Loyalty Program Coordinator deploys satisfaction survey to all active trade account holders via SMS/email; (b) survey covers: (i) lounge amenities rating; (ii) store service quality for trade customers; (iii) product availability for trade essentials; (iv) pricing competitiveness vs. local hardware stores; (v) Net Promoter Score (NPS); (c) response target: &gt; 30% of active accounts; (d) results analyzed by store cluster and trade tier; (e) stores with NPS &lt; 30 flagged for Store Manager coaching; (f) top-rated stores recognized in monthly trade newsletter
Responsible (R): Loyalty Program Coordinator / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1493_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1493_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1493_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1493_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1493_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-268 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Amenities &amp; Assistance (PA-09.3).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
